# shellcheck shell=bash
# scripts/android/versions.env -- every pinned version and revision of the Android build.
#
# Sourced by scripts/android/env.sh (plain KEY=VALUE, bash syntax). Change a pin here and
# the matching build step's stamp no longer matches, so the next run rebuilds that step.
#
# Where the pins come from
# ------------------------
# Third-party versions follow what the desktop Logos closure links (nixpkgs e9f00bd, the
# nixpkgs every Logos flake below pins), so Android runs the same library versions as the
# desktop reference. Exceptions are noted inline.
#
# Logos revisions are the working desktop closure: logos-liblogos db45024, as built and run
# by logos-logoscore-cli 6a0a2f4 (the logoscore used by the desktop probe/harness, see
# docs/investigation.md "Revisions examined"). Most of them are liblogos db45024's own
# flake.lock root inputs. ONE deliberate exception, logos-package-manager / logos-package:
#
#   liblogos db45024's own lock says  lpm d88abaa -> logos-package 49151f0.
#   logoscore 6a0a2f4 overrides it:   lpm d3af297 -> logos-package 4cdb302
#   (`logos-liblogos.inputs.logos-package-manager.follows`), and that is what the desktop
#   runtime actually ran.
#
#   49151f0's liblgx does not export lgx_resolve_main, lgx_free_main_file,
#   lgx_variant_spellings, lgx_host_variant, lgx_verify_installed(_tree), all of which
#   logos-module f71d16d (ALSO pinned by liblogos db45024, linked into liblogos_core)
#   calls. glibc's lazy binding hides that on desktop until the call; bionic binds every
#   symbol at dlopen, so liblogos_core.so would not even load. 4cdb302 has all of them, and
#   it is the revision the platform-ICU patches (patches/logos-package/0001, 0002) were
#   written and tested against (docs/research/exp-lgx-icu.md). So: lpm d3af297 +
#   logos-package 4cdb302. lpm d88abaa..d3af297 changes no CMake/build file.
#
# Resolved with .work/scripts/m2-deps-revs.sh from the fresh clones' flake.lock files.

# --- Target -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# minSdk of the app. The whole prefix must be built at minSdk (bionic API detection at
# build time: statx, pthread_cond_clockwait, ELF TLS), and liblgx's platform ICU needs 31+.
ANDROID_API_DEFAULT=34
NDK_VERSION=r27c                     # Pkg.Revision 27.2.12479018 (source.properties)
QT_VERSION=6.11.1                    # official Android prebuilts (aqt), 16 KB-aligned
AQTINSTALL_VERSION=3.3.0             # installs them (scripts/android/install-qt.sh)

# --- Third-party (built by scripts/android/build-deps.sh) ----------------------------
BOOST_VERSION=1.87.0
BOOST_TARBALL=boost_1_87_0.tar.bz2
BOOST_URL=https://archives.boost.io/release/1.87.0/source/boost_1_87_0.tar.bz2
BOOST_SHA256=af57be25cb4c4f4b413ed692fe378affb4352ea50fbe294a11ef548f4d527d89
# Components liblogos + the Logos runtime use (process, filesystem via Boost::process and
# the Qt loader; context/atomic/date_time are Boost.Process/Asio link deps).
BOOST_LIBS="process filesystem system context atomic date_time"

FMT_VERSION=10.2.1
FMT_URL=https://github.com/fmtlib/fmt/archive/refs/tags/10.2.1.tar.gz
FMT_SHA256=1250e4cc58bf06ee631567523f48848dc4596133e163f02615c97f78bab6c811

SPDLOG_VERSION=1.15.2                # built against the external fmt, shared (as nixpkgs)
SPDLOG_URL=https://github.com/gabime/spdlog/archive/refs/tags/v1.15.2.tar.gz
SPDLOG_SHA256=7a80896357f3e8e920e85e92633b14ba0f229c506e6f978578bdc35ba09e9a5d

NLOHMANN_JSON_VERSION=3.11.3
NLOHMANN_JSON_URL=https://github.com/nlohmann/json/archive/refs/tags/v3.11.3.tar.gz
NLOHMANN_JSON_SHA256=0d8ef5af7f9794e3263480193c491549b2ba6cc74bb018906202ada498a79406

# CLI11: needed by logos-module-loader-qt (logos_host_qt's command-line parser,
# find_package(CLI11 REQUIRED)); no other Logos component uses it. nixpkgs e9f00bd: 2.5.0.
CLI11_VERSION=2.5.0
CLI11_URL=https://github.com/CLIUtils/CLI11/archive/refs/tags/v2.5.0.tar.gz
CLI11_SHA256=17e02b4cddc2fa348e5dbdbb582c59a3486fa2b2433e70a0c3bacb871334fd55

# cpp-semver: header-only dependency of liblgx (include/logos/semver.hpp). Installed into
# the prefix so liblgx's find_package(semver 0.4.0) hits and nothing is fetched at
# configure time. Same tag logos-package's nix/cpp-semver.nix pins (rev b2f4696).
CPP_SEMVER_VERSION=0.4.0
CPP_SEMVER_URL=https://github.com/z4kn4fein/cpp-semver/archive/refs/tags/v0.4.0.tar.gz
CPP_SEMVER_SHA256=9885062b640a4a26dbefa1a07f9c1f0a0e092762d13f2974fdf3fdf0c01ced8d

# OpenSSL: one copy serves both the Logos libraries (logos-protocol / logos-module-loader-qt
# find_package(OpenSSL)) and QtNetwork's TLS backend, which dlopen()s it on Android
# (qtbase 6.11.1 src/plugins/tls/openssl/qsslsocket_openssl_symbols.cpp: first
# "libssl.so.3", which an APK cannot carry, then "ssl" + ANDROID_OPENSSL_SUFFIX, default
# "_3" -> libssl_3.so / libcrypto_3.so). So the libraries are built with the SONAMEs
# libssl_3.so / libcrypto_3.so (the Qt-for-Android / KDAB android_openssl naming), and
# unversioned libssl.so / libcrypto.so symlinks in the prefix let CMake's FindOpenSSL
# link them (the linker records the SONAME, so every NEEDED is libssl_3.so /
# libcrypto_3.so). 3.5 is the current LTS series (nixpkgs e9f00bd ships 3.5.1); the
# latest 3.5.x patch release is used for its security fixes.
OPENSSL_VERSION=3.5.4
OPENSSL_URL=https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/download/openssl-3.5.4/openssl-3.5.4.tar.gz
OPENSSL_SHA256=967311f84955316969bdb1d8d4b983718ef42338639c621ec4c34fddef355e99
# Matches the release's published checksum file (checked by build-deps.sh whenever the pin
# above is emptied, e.g. when bumping the version).
OPENSSL_SHA256_URL=https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/download/openssl-3.5.4/openssl-3.5.4.tar.gz.sha256
OPENSSL_SONAME_SUFFIX=_3             # must match Qt's default ANDROID_OPENSSL_SUFFIX

LIBSODIUM_VERSION=1.0.20             # static, only liblgx uses it
LIBSODIUM_URL=https://download.libsodium.org/libsodium/releases/libsodium-1.0.20.tar.gz
LIBSODIUM_URL_ALT=https://github.com/jedisct1/libsodium/releases/download/1.0.20-RELEASE/libsodium-1.0.20.tar.gz
LIBSODIUM_SHA256=ebb65ef6ca439333c2bb41a0c1990587288da07f6c7fd07cb3a18cc18d30ce19

# zlib: not built; liblgx links the NDK sysroot's libz.so (zlib 1.3.0.1 in NDK r27c,
# a public NDK library since API 21). ICU: not built; liblgx links the platform
# libicu.so (NDK stub, API 31+) via patches/logos-package/0001+0002.

# --- Logos (github.com/logos-co/<repo>) ------------------------------------------------
# liblgx + package_manager_lib are built by build-deps.sh (M2); the rest by M3.
LOGOS_PACKAGE_REV=4cdb302051ebcd231eeaeeaa2011fcf857541ce4          # liblgx (see header)
LOGOS_PACKAGE_MANAGER_REV=d3af2972f51d9c542537d80d60ad8d20282ddcd1  # package_manager_lib (see header)
# Apply patches/logos-package/0003 (lgx_host_variant() -> android-x86_64 / android-arm64)?
# Off: module manifests stay keyed linux-x86_64[-dev], which liblgx reports under bionic.
LGX_ANDROID_VARIANT_PATCH=0
# package_manager_lib portable build (LGPM_PORTABLE_BUILD): selects portable instead of
# -dev variants. Off = liblogos's default `lib` output (LOGOS_PORTABLE_BUILD off too).
LGPM_PORTABLE_BUILD=OFF

LOGOS_LIBLOGOS_REV=db45024f5c45ce5fc00ab76a6921985839ad7355
LOGOS_PROTOCOL_REV=8bbc027c99505c3c2f043265f8c1ae8ff899bdff          # 0.9.0
LOGOS_PLUGIN_QT_REV=3a471be14af66d099827ee712ec8c40ead701340         # logos-qt-host runtime
LOGOS_QT_SDK_REV=03e489b16f9401526e52c0fdbc1e72cbf9fb1144
LOGOS_CPP_SDK_REV=3f34c0b216c8fbdbf2093056b9f0fc53d89f05a1
LOGOS_CONTAINER_REV=641d21108781a353eed9f0567f15776fee06af40
LOGOS_CONTAINER_SUBPROCESS_REV=697c1805eae689fc5945d2afe7038a4b608df07f
LOGOS_MODULE_LOADER_REV=3628b97a32cb2edb30e7d26c0c5113a487e3e993
LOGOS_MODULE_LOADER_QT_REV=888da92cfed51f8039efb11c8a1cbdcb38d04e37  # logos_host_qt
# logos-module appears twice in the closure, and M3 builds both, as the desktop closure
# did: liblogos_core links f71d16d (its root input, which resolves `main` through liblgx);
# logos_host_qt links 9812dc8 (logos-module-loader-qt's own lock; liblogos does not make
# that input follow, and 9812dc8 predates the liblgx dependency). Both are static
# libraries, so each image carries its own copy. Their interface.h is identical, which is
# the header module plugins compile against (from the f71d16d install).
LOGOS_MODULE_REV=f71d16ddc5779b50b188b3a3928a37c9ce90b2a1
LOGOS_MODULE_REV_LOADER_QT=9812dc8c69cfbfed3eea06510a5c1ff33c1fcf7f
PROCESS_STATS_REV=6e0aade77db1b03cc08559c5700c687fa6f00269
# Modules. capability_module (liblogos db45024's bundled module, version 1.0.0) is built
# with logos-module-builder de169fd, the builder its own lock names; hello_module (this
# repo) uses the same builder. modules_state (liblogos' other bundled module) is optional
# at start-up and not built.
LOGOS_CAPABILITY_MODULE_REV=1a1b8b5a1167931afbf41ebaafbe76034e6357a0
LOGOS_MODULES_STATE_MODULE_REV=ed0f4ba534520542764775efc1d0ef705a02e616
LOGOS_MODULE_BUILDER_REV=de169fd45d7bdf6e28ce1f151b4c34880523ace9
# Host code generators (build-runtime.sh step gen): logos-cpp-generator comes from
# logos-cpp-sdk above, logos-qt-host-generator from logos-plugin-qt above; both link the
# LIDL frontend at this rev (cpp-sdk 3f34c0b's and plugin-qt 3a471be's lock).
LOGOS_LIDL_REV=9df8e00372a07e073a17096fd92a62d69c5a21cd
LOGOS_NIX_REV=f55bf91b8a723ee5c27c39c773b034255538d280               # reference only
NIXPKGS_REV=e9f00bd893984bc8ce46c895c3bf7cac95331127                 # reference only
